+// The heads of one KV group and a block of positions walk the KV cells together: a K/V row is read once per block,
+// not once per query (in one_chunk every query walks the whole cache again). The arithmetic of each query is exactly
+// one_chunk: the same functions and expressions, the cells in the same order; the result is bitwise the same.
+static constexpr int64_t FA_GROUP_MAXQ = 40; // queries (position x head) per block: Q and the accumulators stay in L1
